@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`

-- g6-schedule-three.l4: s.41 (the Commissioner's power to impose a financial sanction in the amount of
-- column B of the Third Schedule, and the Minister's power to change the Schedule within a cap) and the
-- Third Schedule itself, as data.
--
-- What this module assumes (PLAN IP14, IP16; each is stated in FRAGMENT-G6.md):
--   * No order under s.41(b) has changed the Third Schedule: the Schedule as enacted (Sefer HaChukim 3349,
--     p. 205) is the only vintage modelled.  An order's content is an INPUT to the s.41(b) power.
--   * Chapter 6 has commenced for the violation: that is the input `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act`
--     (G7 decides it under s.63(b)).  Before it, no sanction may be imposed.
--   * That a violation occurred is decided by G1 (ss.3, 4), G3 (ss.13, 18) and G5 (s.31(2)), and arrives as
--     domain.l4's `Violation`.
--
-- Money is in new shekels, as a bare NUMBER: the Law's column B is headed "in new shekels".

§ `Chapter 6: administrative enforcement measures`

§§ `Subchapter A: imposing a financial sanction`

§§§ `s 41: the acts the section confers`

@desc The acts s.41 confers: the Commissioner's imposing a sanction in the amount the Third Schedule fixes, and the Minister's changing the Schedule by order; the first field says who performs the act
DECLARE `Act under s 41` IS ONE OF
    `impose the financial sanction the Third Schedule fixes for the breach` HAS `performed by the imposing officer` IS A Party
    `change the Third Schedule by order` HAS `performed by the ordering Minister` IS A Party

§§§ `The Third Schedule: column A and column B, items (1) to (7)`

-- Each item is one row.  The corporation column prints a dash for items (1), (2) and (4); a dash is NOTHING,
-- never zero and never the individual amount (trap T14).
-- Columns of the rows below:    item, violation,                                                 provision,      individual,   corporation

-- src:702 | {{ח:ת}} <table width="100%">
-- src:703 | <tr><th rowspan="2">{{מוקטן|טור א׳}} {{ש}} ההוראה</th><th colspan="2" width="200px">{{מוקטן|טור ב׳}} {{ש}} סכום העיצום הכספי {{ש}} (בשקלים חדשים)</th></tr>
-- src:704 | <tr><th>יחיד</th><th>תאגיד</th></tr>
-- src:705 | <tr id="תוספת 3 פרט 1"><td>
-- src:706 | {{ח:תת|(1)}} עוסק שביצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידו רישיון כלל, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 3|סעיף 3(א)}};
-- src:707 | </td><td>20,000</td><td>—</td></tr>
@ref Third Schedule item (1) (src:702-707)
GIVETH A `Third Schedule row`
`Third Schedule item (1)` MEANS
    `Third Schedule row` OF 1, `work with no licence at all`,                                  `contravenes section 3(a)`,  JUST 20_000, NOTHING

-- src:708 | <tr id="תוספת 3 פרט 2"><td>
-- src:709 | {{ח:תת|(2)}} ביצע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידו רישיון מהסוג המתאים לביצוע פעולה באותה מערכת, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 3|סעיף 3(א)}};
-- src:710 | </td><td>10,000</td><td>—</td></tr>
@ref Third Schedule item (2) (src:708-710)
GIVETH A `Third Schedule row`
`Third Schedule item (2)` MEANS
    `Third Schedule row` OF 2, `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`, `contravenes section 3(a)`,  JUST 10_000, NOTHING

-- src:711 | <tr id="תוספת 3 פרט 3"><td>
-- src:712 | {{ח:תת|(3)}} פרסם עצמו כבעל רישיון בלי שיש בידו רישיון או פרסם עצמו כבעל רישיון מסוג מסוים בלי שיש בידו רישיון מאותו סוג, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 4|סעיף 4}};
-- src:713 | </td><td>5,000</td><td>10,000</td></tr>
@ref Third Schedule item (3) (src:711-713)
GIVETH A `Third Schedule row`
`Third Schedule item (3)` MEANS
    `Third Schedule row` OF 3, `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`,     `contravenes section 4`,     JUST 5_000,  JUST 10_000

-- src:714 | <tr id="תוספת 3 פרט 4"><td>
-- src:715 | {{ח:תת|(4)}} בעל רישיון שביצע התקנה של מערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי לבצע בדיקת אטימות לצנרת חומר הקירור בהתאם להוראות הקבועות בפרק הבדיקות בתקן ישראלי ת״י 994 חלק 4 – מזגני אוויר: התקנה, בניגוד להוראת {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 13|סעיף 13}};
-- src:716 | </td><td>20,000</td><td>—</td></tr>
@ref Third Schedule item (4) (src:714-716)
GIVETH A `Third Schedule row`
`Third Schedule item (4)` MEANS
    `Third Schedule row` OF 4, `installation without the tightness test of the piping`,       `contravenes section 13`,    JUST 20_000, NOTHING

-- src:717 | <tr id="תוספת 3 פרט 5"><td>
-- src:718 | {{ח:תת|(5)}} מפעיל שהפעיל אדם אחר בביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידי אותו אדם רישיון כלל, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 18|סעיף 18(א)}};
-- src:719 | </td><td>20,000</td><td>40,000</td></tr>
@ref Third Schedule item (5) (src:717-719)
GIVETH A `Third Schedule row`
`Third Schedule item (5)` MEANS
    `Third Schedule row` OF 5, `engaging a person who had no licence at all`,                 `contravenes section 18(a)`, JUST 20_000, JUST 40_000

-- src:720 | <tr id="תוספת 3 פרט 6"><td>
-- src:721 | {{ח:תת|(6)}} מפעיל שהפעיל אדם אחר בביצוע עבודה במערכת קירור או מיזוג אוויר בלי שיש בידי אותו אדם רישיון מהסוג המתאים לביצוע עבודה באותה מערכת, בניגוד להוראות {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 18|סעיף 18(א)}};
-- src:722 | </td><td>10,000</td><td>20,000</td></tr>
@ref Third Schedule item (6) (src:720-722)
GIVETH A `Third Schedule row`
`Third Schedule item (6)` MEANS
    `Third Schedule row` OF 6, `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`, `contravenes section 18(a)`, JUST 10_000, JUST 20_000

-- src:723 | <tr id="תוספת 3 פרט 7"><td>
-- src:724 | {{ח:תת|(7)}} לא מסר מסמך לפי דרישת מפקח שניתנה לפי {{ח:פנימי|סעיף 31|סעיף 31(2)}}.
-- src:725 | </td><td>3,000</td><td>6,000</td></tr>
@ref Third Schedule item (7) (src:723-725)
GIVETH A `Third Schedule row`
`Third Schedule item (7)` MEANS
    `Third Schedule row` OF 7, `failing to give a document an inspector demanded`,            `contravenes section 31(2)`, JUST 3_000,  JUST 6_000

@ref Third Schedule items (1) to (7) (src:705-725)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Third Schedule row`
`the Third Schedule` MEANS
    LIST `Third Schedule item (1)`
       , `Third Schedule item (2)`
       , `Third Schedule item (3)`
       , `Third Schedule item (4)`
       , `Third Schedule item (5)`
       , `Third Schedule item (6)`
       , `Third Schedule item (7)`

-- The row of a listed violation: `Listed violation` has one constructor for each of the seven items.
@ref Third Schedule items (1) to (7) (src:705-725)
GIVEN violation IS A `Listed violation`
GIVETH A `Third Schedule row`
`Third Schedule — the row for` violation MEANS
    CONSIDER violation
    WHEN `work with no licence at all`                                  THEN `Third Schedule item (1)`
    WHEN `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system` THEN `Third Schedule item (2)`
    WHEN `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`      THEN `Third Schedule item (3)`
    WHEN `installation without the tightness test of the piping`        THEN `Third Schedule item (4)`
    WHEN `engaging a person who had no licence at all`                  THEN `Third Schedule item (5)`
    WHEN `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`  THEN `Third Schedule item (6)`
    WHEN `failing to give a document an inspector demanded`             THEN `Third Schedule item (7)`

-- The provision a violation contravenes, from the last clause of column A.  s.45(b) says "the same
-- provision" and items (1) and (2) both contravene s.3(a), items (5) and (6) both s.18(a) (trap T17).
@ref Third Schedule column A, last clause of each item (src:705-725)
GIVEN violation IS A `Listed violation`
GIVETH A `Provision contravened`
`Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` violation MEANS
    (`Third Schedule — the row for` violation)'s `the provision contravened`

§§§ `s 41(a): the amount fixed in column B`

-- Column B of the Third Schedule: the amount set beside the item, for an individual or a corporation.
-- NOTHING is the dash.  A MAYBE, not a refusal, at this level: the table says exactly what the Law prints.
-- src:342 | {{ח:סעיף|41|עיצום כספי}}
-- src:343 | {{ח:תת|(א)}} הפר אדם הוראה מההוראות לפי חוק זה, כמפורט {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 3|בטור א׳ בתוספת השלישית}}, רשאי עובד בכיר של המשרד שהשר הסמיכו לעניין {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק זה}} ({{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|בפרק זה}} – הממונה), להטיל עליו עיצום כספי לפי הוראות {{ח:פנימי|פרק ו|פרק זה}}, בסכום הקבוע בטור ב׳ לצידה.
@ref s.41(a), Third Schedule column B (src:343, src:702-725)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
      violation IS A `Listed violation`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `the kind of person` `and` violation MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of person`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN (`Third Schedule — the row for` violation)'s `column B for an individual`
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN (`Third Schedule — the row for` violation)'s `column B for a corporation`

-- The dash is the one place where the Law prints no figure, and s.41(a) says the amount is "the amount set in
-- column B beside it".  The Law does not say whether a dash means no sanction may be imposed, or that a figure
-- was left out; so the answer is a named refusal, never zero and never the individual amount.
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`s 41(a) — column B sets no amount here, and the Law does not say whether a dash means that no sanction may be imposed or that a figure was left out` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 41(a) — column B sets no amount here, and the Law does not say whether a dash means that no sanction may be imposed or that a figure was left out"

-- "in the amount set in column B beside it": the fixed sanction, as enacted (before any s.45 addition or
-- s.47 update).  A dash is returned as the named refusal above, in return position, so nothing can default it.
-- src:343 is the sentence whose last words this encodes; src:702-725 is the table.
@ref s.41(a), Third Schedule column B (src:343, src:702-725)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
      violation IS A `Listed violation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `the kind of person` `and` violation MEANS
    CONSIDER (`s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `the kind of person` `and` violation)
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 41(a) — column B sets no amount here, and the Law does not say whether a dash means that no sanction may be imposed or that a figure was left out`

@ref s.41(a), Third Schedule column B (src:343, src:702-725)
@export The amount in new shekels that column B of the Third Schedule, as enacted, fixes for a violation, by the kind of person who committed it; a named refusal at a dash (a corporation at items (1), (2) and (4))
GIVEN violation IS A Violation @desc One act that breached a listed provision: who committed it (an individual or a corporation), which Third Schedule item it breached, the act's reference and its day
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` violation MEANS
    `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` (violation's `the violator`'s `kind of person`) `and` (violation's `the listed violation`)

§§§ `s 41(a): the Commissioner's power`

-- "a senior employee of the Ministry whom the Minister authorised for this chapter (in this chapter, the
-- Commissioner)": who holds the office is an input.  "Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act" is G7's
-- answer under s.63(b).  The three limbs are ordered so that the Law's own earlier answers come first: a
-- violation before Chapter 6 commenced is not sanctionable whatever column B says, so the dash of a
-- corporation's cell is reached only when the other two limbs hold.
@ref s.41(a) (src:343)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(a) — column B sets an amount for` violation MEANS
    CONSIDER (`s 41(a) — column B sets, for` (violation's `the violator`'s `kind of person`) `and` (violation's `the listed violation`))
    WHEN JUST amount THEN TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `s 41(a) — column B sets no amount here, and the Law does not say whether a dash means that no sanction may be imposed or that a figure was left out`

@ref s.41(a) (src:342-343)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` violation `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6` MEANS
        `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act`
    AND `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6`
    AND `s 41(a) — column B sets an amount for` violation

-- The alternative reading of a dash (fork F-DASH): a dash means that no sanction may be imposed on that kind of person
-- for that item.  Callable here; it answers FALSE where the taken reading refuses.
@ref s.41(a) (src:343)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` violation `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6` MEANS
        `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act`
    AND `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6`
    AND isJust (`s 41(a) — column B sets, for` (violation's `the violator`'s `kind of person`) `and` (violation's `the listed violation`))

@ref s.41(a) (src:343)
GIVEN violation IS A Violation
      `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under s 41`
`s 41(a) — the Commissioner may impose the financial sanction for` violation `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6` MEANS
    IF   `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` violation `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` `the Commissioner holds the Minister's authorisation for Chapter 6`
    THEN PARTY `the Commissioner`
         MAY   `impose the financial sanction the Third Schedule fixes for the breach` `the Commissioner`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `s 41(b): the Minister's power to change the Third Schedule, and its cap`

-- "not exceed 40,000 new shekels, and if the violator is a corporation, 80,000 new shekels".
-- The cap bounds the amount an ORDER may set in column B.  It does not bound what is payable after s.45
-- additions and s.47 updates (trap T15; see FRAGMENT-G6.md, fork on the cap).
-- src:344 | {{ח:תת|(ב)}} השר, בהסכמת שר המשפטים, ובאישור ועדת העבודה והרווחה של הכנסת, רשאי לשנות, בצו, את {{ח:פנימי|תוספת 3|התוספת השלישית}}, ובלבד שסכום העיצום הכספי שייקבע בטור ב׳ שבה, לא יעלה על 40,000 שקלים חדשים, ואם המפר הוא תאגיד – על 80,000 שקלים חדשים.
@ref s.41(b) (src:344)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for an individual` MEANS 40_000

@ref s.41(b) (src:344)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for a corporation` MEANS 80_000

@ref s.41(b) (src:344)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for` `the kind of person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of person`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN `s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for an individual`
    WHEN `a corporation` THEN `s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for a corporation`

-- "shall not exceed": AT MOST, so the cap itself is allowed.  A dash sets no amount and so exceeds nothing.
@ref s.41(b) (src:344)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `Person kind`
      cell IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `the kind of person` `holding` cell MEANS
    CONSIDER cell
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST amount THEN amount AT MOST `s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for` `the kind of person`

@ref s.41(b) (src:344)
GIVEN row IS A `Third Schedule row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(b) — both column B cells of the row are within the cap` row MEANS
        `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `an individual` `holding` (row's `column B for an individual`)
    AND `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `a corporation` `holding` (row's `column B for a corporation`)

@ref s.41(b) (src:344)
GIVEN rows IS A LIST OF `Third Schedule row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(b) — every row is within the cap` rows MEANS
    all (GIVEN row YIELD `s 41(b) — both column B cells of the row are within the cap` row) rows

-- The Minister's power: with the Minister of Justice's consent and the approval of the Knesset Labour and
-- Welfare Committee, by order, provided the amounts set stay within the cap.  Consent and approval are facts
-- (inputs); the order's content is the list of rows it would set.
@ref s.41(b) (src:344)
GIVEN `the rows the order would set` IS A LIST OF `Third Schedule row`
      `the Minister of Justice consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` `the rows the order would set` `the Minister of Justice consented` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` MEANS
        `the Minister of Justice consented`
    AND `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order`
    AND `s 41(b) — every row is within the cap` `the rows the order would set`

@ref s.41(b) (src:344)
GIVEN `the rows the order would set` IS A LIST OF `Third Schedule row`
      `the Minister of Justice consented` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `Act under s 41`
`s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by order` `the rows the order would set` `the Minister of Justice consented` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order` MEANS
    IF   `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` `the rows the order would set` `the Minister of Justice consented` `the Knesset Labour and Welfare Committee approved the order`
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY   `change the Third Schedule by order` `the Minister`
    ELSE FULFILLED
